 "note": "TEST_EXISTING v7 target (public-test-case-existing-v7): 16 exported functions from 15 permissive repos outside lm-corpus (repo and module sha checked against ext-manifest 8458eac6 + ext-corpus.json), each called by an existing test file at the pinned commit (HEAD of the clone), where v1-v6 refuse the function (test_target_signature) and v7 accepts it on the pinned module text, following relative imports only through the pinned sibling fixtures (4 examples need a sibling). The examples cover both v7 widenings: 10 take or return a global Map / ReadonlyMap / Set / ReadonlySet with string or number keys and plain-data values, and 6 return void (assert-style validators; checks may only be throws or is undefined, with at least one throws). Method: the HEAD scan of the same 411 + 326 cloned permissive TypeScript repos used for M88-M93, replaying every candidate on the full clone with the v7 closure rules (load-time reach, non-.ts relative imports, require / dynamic import, import-back, global patching, container escapes), found 73 candidates (3 in Peace's repos, dropped); 64 replay and pass the license and size (64 KiB) checks, 56 of those pass the pre-push core-text scan (about 20 more accept only through a Map / Set nested in an interface or alias, which v7 also covers). Kept one example per repo where possible, smallest first, with the Map / Set or void visible in the signature (awslabs/aidlc-workflows gives one of each). Peace's public repos were checked first (see peace): PeaceSTOCKS has fitting functions, but it is in the corpus manifest, so they are recorded and not counted.",
